      {
        "Id": "9272c9fad00444e2a250ae955e025446",
        "Title": "PRELIMINARY PROPOSAL - NOT CHECKED BY A STRUCTURAL ENGINEER.  HOW TO USE: open the architectural floor plan.  Run ANALYSE (0): reads walls / rooms / floors / stairs / grids / levels, proposes columns by engineering rules (corners, free ends, cuts of spans longer than input 6; NOT every wall intersection), takes loads down floor by floor, sizes beams / columns / footings and saves report.txt + members.csv in Documents\\SD_Structural_Genius.  Footings need the SOIL data (11, 12) from the geotechnical report - never assumed.  PREVIEW draws lines only.  GENERATE builds native columns, plinth / floor / roof / stair beams and footings ONLY for what you approve (25-27) and switched on (18-24); every element says PROPOSED - B25.  Rerun = replaced; Ctrl+Z undoes a run; DELETE removes B25 elements.  Wind, frame analysis, detailing, raft / piles, two-way slab strength = NOT DONE (see the report).",
        "DescriptionText": "",
        "IsExpanded": true,
        "WidthAdjustment": 0.0,
        "HeightAdjustment": 0.0,
        "Nodes": [],
        "HasNestedGroups": false,
        "Left": 0.0,
